# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the vendored Node.js tests (QJSNAPI_SANITIZE).
#
# Only leaks that the Node.js tests make by design belong here: a napi_ref
# owned by the addon (ReferenceOwnership::kUserland) that the addon never
# deletes. Node.js leaks the same reference; it just does not run its tests
# under LeakSanitizer. Every entry names the function that creates the leaked
# reference, so a leak anywhere else is still reported.

# test_reference/test_finalizer.c: when the JS finalizer throws (the point of
# the test), FinalizeExternalCallJs returns at NODE_API_CALL_RETURN_VOID
# before napi_delete_reference(finalizer_ref).
leak:CreateExternalWithJsFinalize

# test_reference_double_free/test_reference_double_free.c: `new
# MyObject(false)` wraps with NoDeleteDestructor, which frees its malloc'ed
# holder but never deletes the napi_ref returned by napi_wrap.
leak:test_reference_double_free.c
